Patch summary:
gfxstream's guest stops spinning through long waits for the host. A thread
waiting for a reply, for the host to drain the command ring or for room in it
yielded the CPU in a loop and only began to sleep after 50 million passes, so
it kept a vCPU busy for the whole wait: the composer, which waits for the host
to compose every frame, used 33-44% of a vCPU during 3DMark Sling Shot
Extreme. Now a wait spins for its first 200 us, as fast replies come back in
microseconds, then sleeps between polls in steps doubling up to 200 us. The
loop in type1Write that waits for room in the ring, which did not even yield,
uses the same backoff, and every wait starts its own spin window.

